WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
Humanoid robot DRAM Demand is projected to rise 20 fold by 2030. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.120
631. Demand for DRAM chips in humanoid robots is forecast to grow 20 times larger by 2030 according

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:19.880
to Chosun. The surge ties directly to rising production and deployment of AI-driven robots.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:25.320
The growth reflects the increasing complexity of AI systems that require substantial memory

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.120
for processing sensor data and controlling movements in real time.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.320
Tesla updated its European site to label the original straight line summon feature as

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:34.960
dumb summon.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.840
The feature now sits inside the Tesla-assisted driving basic package, priced at 99 euros

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.800
per month, and includes auto-steer plus navigate on auto-steer.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.060
The change aligns with Tesla's broader rebranding of driver assistance features in the region,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.180
following regulatory discussions, according to NOT a Tesla app.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:01:01.380
A 2020 Model Y lost its high-voltage battery at 65,000 miles without any prior alerts or warnings.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.060
The owner noted the failure occurred while the vehicle remained under Tesla's battery

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:11.320
warranty, though the incident raises questions about long-term reliability once coverage ends.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.460
The case highlights the importance of warranty coverage for early high-voltage battery issues

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.100
in Model Y vehicles, according to torque news.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:25.240
Construction has begun in Arizona on Project Sterling, a large solar-plus storage facility

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.440
whose annual output Tesla will buy at a rate of about 90%.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.780
Developer Contour Global announced the start of onsite work on October 7th, 2026, and is

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.580
aiming for commercial operation in 2028.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:46.380
The plan pairs 450 megawatts of AC solar capacity with a 1.4 gigawatts hour battery, and

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.660
And the company says it can supply power for up to 16 hours a day.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.760
The project's defining feature is its design to shift daytime solar generation into the

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.480
hours after sunset and deliver it to the California market as well.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.640
The site is in the Mojave Desert in Mojave County, Arizona, north of Lake Havasu City, according

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.700
to Xeno Spectrum.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.800
Tesla is finally letting its two most popular electric cars send power back into the

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:11.880
house during an outage.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:17.380
New Model 3 and Model Y buyers in the US and Puerto Rico can tap the feature as long

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.480
as the home also has a Powerwall 3.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.560
Until now, Tesla only offered that capability on the Cybertruck.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.800
According to Tesla's revised PowerShare page, the feature is currently available for all

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.760
Cybertruck vehicles and all new Model 3 and Model Y vehicles ordered on October 1, 2026

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.920
or later, Electric reported.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.640
That means outage backup depends on more than the vehicle alone.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.120
The setup also needs a compatible charger and a home with Powerwall 3.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:51.340
For a home that uses 30 kilowatt hours per day, Tesla says a Model 3 or Model Y starting

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:56.660
at 90% charge can provide over two days of added backup, while standard trims offer

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.560
up to two days.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.720
The company rates the setup for a maximum continuous output of 11.52 kilowatts according

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:04.840
to Yahoo autos.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.640
Tesla's full self-driving feature could be heading to Europe's roads sooner rather than

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:15.360
later, but German regulators are insisting on a name change. In a post published by Germany's

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.340
Federal Ministry of Transport, Minister Stefan Bilger said he is advocating for swift approval

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.940
of the feature in the EU. However, the ministry insists that the current name FSD is somewhat

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:31.380
misleading, as the car does not take over the entire driving process. While the system can

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:37.140
accelerate, break and steer, the human driver must supervise it at all times and remains responsible.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.500
As a result, Tesla has reportedly offered to rename the system Tesla assisted driving.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.000
The name of the feature itself hasn't been the only roadblock on the way to approval.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.400
Bilger says that many technical aspects as well as issues surrounding liability still need

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.980
to be resolved, though he said he reached a common understanding and a constructive agreement

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.940
after meeting with the firm in September.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.920
My goal is for Tesla drivers to be able to benefit from assisted driving throughout the

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.180
EU as quickly as possible, said Bilger.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.720
At the time of writing, FSD has been approved in eight European countries.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:16.660
The Netherlands, Belgium, Denmark, Lithuania, Estonia, Slovenia, Czechia, and Croatia.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:21.480
An EU-wide vote is expected not before December, according to PC Mag.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:28.460
Tesla-China-made EV sales rise 5% in September, extending growth streak to 11 months despite

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.700
global sales slump.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:34.660
The increase marks the 11th consecutive month of growth for China-made Tesla vehicles.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:39.360
levels. The rise occurred even as global EV sales faced broader pressure, according

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:46.860
to Yahoo Finance. Tesla started distributing map update NA 2026.38 across North America.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.340
The package adds updated roads, points of interest, speed limits, and lane guidance data.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:05:04.640
The update follows NA 2026.26 by just over two months, according to not a Tesla app. Tesla

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.220
yet again. The delay continues the pattern of postponed reveals for the high-performance

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:14.800
vehicle according to MoneyWise.com. Tesla says Optimus learned to do chores just by

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.760
watching humans on video. The development shows progress in the robot's ability to learn

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:25.200
from visual demonstrations according to startup fortune. Tesla's CyberCab is coming to Dallas

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.500
soon, exec says. The announcement follows the rapid scaling of the fleet in Austin according

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:35.800
to electric vehicles. Community observers counted more than 40 Tesla semis at the Nevada

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:41.020
production site in a single day. The sighting points to continued ramp activity at the facility

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.960
according to the Tesla Motors subreddit. Musk stated that real AI must perform on inputs it has

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:52.560
never seen before without pre-programming. He noted that most competitor robot videos rely on

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:58.120
scripted sequences or remote control. The definition sets a high bar for what qualifies as

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:03.440
genuine artificial intelligence in robotics, according to Basinor. Musk reported that the

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.880
digital-optimus AI has progressed halfway through the Diablo campaign by observing the screen

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.460
like a human player. Training on League of Legends is also underway. The progress demonstrates

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.680
the AI's ability to learn complex game mechanics through visual input alone,

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:24.080
according to Drive Tesla Canada. The case serves as a reminder that battery failures can occur

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.040
without warning, even in relatively new vehicles, according to torque news.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:33.760
Battery demand forecasts for humanoid robots rest on the memory bandwidth required for real-time

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.880
sensor fusion and motor control loops.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:41.840
A 20-fold increase in DRAM consumption by 2030 implies that each additional robot will

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.040
need roughly the same memory footprint as several current data center inference cards.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.360
That scaling changes the cost structure of robot production because memory already accounts

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.580
for a measurable share of bill of materials in high performance AI systems.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:02.060
Manufacturers who secure long-term DRAM supply contracts early can lock in lower per unit costs

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:07.780
while competitors face spot market volatility. The same dynamic appears in electric vehicle

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.440
battery packs where cell chemistry and pack integration determine whether a vehicle reaches

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:18.580
target margins or remains a loss leader at volume. The interplay between memory requirements and

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:23.320
an overall system cost will shape which companies can scale humanoid production profitably.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.400
Early movers in supply agreements may gain a lasting advantage in the emerging market

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:29.280
for these machines.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:34.900
The parallel to EV battery economics shows how component choices ripple through the entire

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.020
product economics.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.440
Securing stable memory supply therefore becomes a strategic priority rather than a simple

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.500
procurement task.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.060
Companies that treat DRAM contracts as core to their robot economics stand to improve gross

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:53.260
margins at scale. The pattern mirrors earlier supply chain lessons in the electric vehicle

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:56.940
sector where cell pricing directly influence vehicle affordability.

